{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788582572466991001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"slowwitted-aspherical-fireant","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"a58c0eafaaebfb98ae1df02f600d10e2827b6675dedb1e6653917fab1148df21","event_uuid":"a5661b84-8e3c-4371-a56e-91b61f04f13c","position":{"commit_sha":"1017150c610f60f6bc1eff09a31794ee28e973c1","position":"1788570134534418243-a5661b84-8e3c-4371-a56e-91b61f04f13c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"c183bef9ed042676031355c05f1e475497edee91203664fbbc67d66a20ed4b9b","event_uuid":"75c9b209-05ea-48bf-b2d6-44deeb79e7b7","position":{"commit_sha":"eda4f540e12b6d22ba19654946703d856d2981cf","position":"1788570141643169094-75c9b209-05ea-48bf-b2d6-44deeb79e7b7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788570134534418243,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"75c9b209-05ea-48bf-b2d6-44deeb79e7b7","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ff4a-2832-def4-4e55"}],"description":"## Context\n\nCarved out of bug `ff4a-2832-def4-4e55` AC5, which asked that the `--status` / claim-gate refusal\n\"state the CHEAP remedy first and unambiguously, so a reader does not default to re-running a\nbillable review\". Left out of ff4a's fix deliberately: ff4a's change is scoped to the proven root\ncause (the async gate daemon losing the op-cert signer binding) plus its sign-time guard, and this\ntouches a different file with a different rationale.\n\n## The current message and why it hedges\n\n`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest_gate.py:141-149` returns both remedies:\n\n> `no certified plan-review attestation (signature: <verdict>; <reason>). Run\n> \\`rebar review-plan <id>\\` to earn one, or \\`rebar sign-review <id>\\` if a review already PASSED\n> but its attestation failed to persist`\n\nThe in-code rationale (bug 94a3) is sound as far as it goes: *\"rebar cannot tell 'never reviewed'\nfrom 'review PASSed but signing aborted' — both leave no record — so name BOTH remedies.\"*\n\n## The improvement — better than a reorder\n\nThat ambiguity is real for `verdict == \"unsigned\"`. It is **not** real for\n`verdict == \"mismatch\"`, which is exactly what ff4a produced:\n\n```\n\"verdict\": \"mismatch\",\n\"reason\": \"... ssh-keygen -Y verify rejected signature (exit 255)\"\n```\n\nA `mismatch` means a signature **exists** and failed to verify. That is unambiguous evidence a\nreview ran and persisted something — so `sign-review` (free, no LLM) is definitively the remedy\nand `review-plan` (15-20 min, billable) is definitively not. Merely reordering the two clauses\nwould still present a choice where none exists.\n\nSo: branch the remedy on `result.get(\"verdict\")` rather than reordering a fixed string.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 - When the signature verdict is `mismatch` (or any verdict that proves a signature was\n      persisted), the refusal names `rebar sign-review <id>` as THE remedy and does not offer\n      `review-plan` as a co-equal alternative.\n- [ ] AC2 - When the verdict is `unsigned` the message keeps naming both remedies, preserving the\n      bug 94a3 behaviour and its stated reasoning.\n- [ ] AC3 - A test covers both branches by verdict, asserting the observable refusal text.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nNot removing `sign-review`. Not changing what the gate scores or when it refuses — message only.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3f5a-2ea8-7041-42a6","ticket_type":"task","title":"Branch the plan-review claim-gate remedy on the signature verdict: a mismatch proves a review happened, so name sign-review unambiguously","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a5661b84-8e3c-4371-a56e-91b61f04f13c","75c9b209-05ea-48bf-b2d6-44deeb79e7b7"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788582572466991001,"uuid":"85c8bb2f-83d1-4e36-87a0-5535a1f7e7cf"}